From 49ec197f169adc9e04c4d5baf7d33f9f04a0e668 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:25:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(post): grblHAL, TinyG and Carvera state the clearance
 Z before the first X/Y traverse

After a tool change (and at the program's start) the three posts wrote a
bare X/Y rapid at whatever height the change left the tip - the #1614
hazard: a long tool on a high work offset can stand below the part top
there. Each now writes a Z-only G0 to the section's ClearancePlane, else
its RetractPlane (never below the move's own Z) before that traverse, as
tormach.cps does in PR #1618. A stream that states neither plane is
refused by name with #1618's wording. A feed's rapid down to its start
height is skipped when the traverse already stated that height.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/first_traverse_clearance.rs. Goldens gain the
one G0 Z line each; test streams that stated no plane now state one, as
post::dump does. The Fanuc family (fanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm,
sinumerik, heidenhain) remains for a second PR.

Refs #1616

